      "worked": "The value before adding $-5$ must be $5$ to make a zero pair. Since $3+2=5$, subtract $-2$. The missing number is $-2$.\n\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}3-(-2)+(-5)&=3+2-5\\\\3-(-2)+(-5)&=5-5\\\\3-(-2)+(-5)&=0\\end{align*}$$",
